From 96e0e41c61657689efb87f703a0ae9a261618810 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hermes <hermes@localhost>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 01:00:20 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 19/21] Link ALAudio through Emscripten WebAudio OpenAL and
 stream Vorbis music

Compile ALAudio plus the vendored Ogg/Vorbis decoder into the browser target
and bind OpenAL against the SDK's WebAudio-backed libopenal; no openal-soft
fallback and no entry-point shims were needed.

Adapt the module to a single-threaded Asyncify runtime: decode Ogg chunks on
the main thread instead of a background pthread, drain every processed stream
buffer per tick, deepen the Emscripten stream queue, resolve the ALFuncs table
against the linked library instead of a DLL handle, disable the voice capture
device (which would open a second AudioContext and call getUserMedia), and keep
queued transient USounds alive across the LoadMap collection.

Expose the real AudioContext, an analyser tap and audioDebug counters to the
browser shell, and let the interactive web client run with sound (the bounded,
splash and Node paths keep -nosound).
